    {
      "id": "claim_71df95f9d54a4278acca6a062fef8dba",
      "statement": "AbstractTLRControllerTest derives the family /start and /start-and-wait endpoint paths from the TraceLinkType passed to its constructor and drives the full start → poll → retrieve lifecycle (runPipeline_start_and_getResult), asserting at each stage both the HTTP status/message pairing and the actual Redis key state via the injected RedisAccessor before cleaning up with deleteResult; re-running start or start-and-wait with the same inputs must return the cached result, pinning the content-based dedup behavior. Its start-and-wait helper accepts either an immediately ready 200 result or a 202 timeout (bounded by tlr.timeout.seconds) and then polls wait-for-result until ready.",
